{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Since quill-server moved to the new Kubernetes cluster, render latency has bad spikes: p99 went from about 2 s to 9 s, while CPU usage looks low, around 1.2 cores of the 2 we give it. Same image as before. Any idea?"},"uuid":"c3c3bfb9-48c5-4df1-bfb4-5036a5cf2d67","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:37.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"c3c3bfb9-48c5-4df1-bfb4-5036a5cf2d67","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01yqryAk6ygSsQFcn42FCHaS","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HONusu5Dzen6TfyVC7afPI","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"kubectl -n quill get deploy quill-server -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].resources}{\"\\n\"}'; kubectl get nodes -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,CPU:.status.capacity.cpu | head -3"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":537,"output_tokens":545}},"uuid":"3f8eb0e4-6509-4cf8-8255-8327138596b3","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:41.000Z","requestId":"req_011CS1IviK3OW0X4YF5tNczh"}
{"parentUuid":"3f8eb0e4-6509-4cf8-8255-8327138596b3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HONusu5Dzen6TfyVC7afPI","content":"{\"limits\":{\"cpu\":\"2\",\"memory\":\"4Gi\"},\"requests\":{\"cpu\":\"2\",\"memory\":\"4Gi\"}}\nNAME            CPU\nk8s-pool-b-01   32\n"}]},"uuid":"cc35682b-d597-4b30-a460-f8a388d1d0b2","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:46.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"cc35682b-d597-4b30-a460-f8a388d1d0b2","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_017WUi1GeOHx9M1YoNky2MSD","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The pod has a CPU limit of 2 and the new nodes have 32 cores. Average CPU use can look low while the container is still being throttled: the limit is enforced as a CFS quota per 100 ms period, and if many threads burn through the quota early in a period, the whole container is paused until the next one. Let me check the throttling counters and what GOMAXPROCS the Go runtime picked."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":857,"output_tokens":497}},"uuid":"8404e2e6-3757-4a08-832f-aa00313aea21","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:55.000Z","requestId":"req_011CDRc5g6hWn0iqPN7WziSl"}
{"parentUuid":"8404e2e6-3757-4a08-832f-aa00313aea21","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01g3s5yBupKlyLzhVAP2mQHR","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01l4quX5vSRPnEtDTno3LK2R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"kubectl -n quill logs deploy/quill-server | grep -m1 gomaxprocs; kubectl -n quill exec deploy/quill-server -- cat /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.stat | grep -E '^[0-9]|nr_periods|nr_throttled'"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":808,"output_tokens":514}},"uuid":"67743bd2-dcb2-4b34-b9f5-3d21fd8bc185","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:56.000Z","requestId":"req_011Cy7WnmSV6KtIMZg5kUmRb"}
{"parentUuid":"67743bd2-dcb2-4b34-b9f5-3d21fd8bc185","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01l4quX5vSRPnEtDTno3LK2R","content":"level=INFO msg=\"runtime\" go=go1.23.4 gomaxprocs=32 numcpu=32\n200000 100000\nnr_periods 418230\nnr_throttled 251377"}]},"uuid":"d445b9de-3c00-4c88-9b83-478417c90c93","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:26:59.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d445b9de-3c00-4c88-9b83-478417c90c93","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01Jj638zj18p88QvMCYPY2TE","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the cause. The binary is built with Go 1.23, and before Go 1.25 the runtime sets GOMAXPROCS to the number of CPUs it sees on the machine, ignoring the container's CPU limit. On these nodes that is 32, sixteen times the limit. With 32 Ps the renderer runs up to 32 threads in parallel, uses up the 200 ms of CPU per 100 ms period (cpu.max 200000 100000) in a few milliseconds, and is then throttled for the rest of the period. 251,377 of 418,230 periods were throttled, 60%. That pause lands on whatever request is in flight, which is the p99.\n\nThe fix is to make GOMAXPROCS match the limit. Options: set the GOMAXPROCS env var from the container's CPU limit with the downward API (resourceFieldRef limits.cpu), add go.uber.org/automaxprocs, or move to Go 1.25, whose runtime reads the cgroup limit itself. The env var is a deploy-only change and works now."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":467,"output_tokens":97}},"uuid":"e7342d4b-5f0e-4b70-9470-0a67f8de6754","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:27:01.000Z","requestId":"req_011CqFeQJB0i03zX0s4b2JcF"}
{"parentUuid":"e7342d4b-5f0e-4b70-9470-0a67f8de6754","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-19","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/render-latency","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Do the env var now. We'll do the Go upgrade separately."},"uuid":"8b3d79ee-9e41-4440-ad2b-8c413742439a","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:27:26.000Z"}
